const status=(text,kind)=>`<span class="pill ${kind||({Pass:'green',Fail:'red',Unknown:'amber',Active:'green',Draft:'amber',Merged:'green',Resolved:'green',Simulated:'blue'}[text]||'')}">${esc(text)}</span>`;
const btn=(text,go,cls='')=>`<button class="pbutton ${cls}" data-go="${go}">${text}</button>`;
const card=(title,content,style='')=>`<div class="panel" ${style?`style="${style}"`:''}><h3>${title}</h3>${content}</div>`;
const row=(a,b,extra='')=>`<div class="minirow"><span>${a}</span><span>${b}</span>${extra}</div>`;
const stat=(name,value,delta,red=false)=>`<div class="stat"><div class="stat-top">${name}</div><span class="stat-v">${value}</span><span class="stat-change ${red?'red':''}">${delta}</span></div>`;
function shell(index,content,crumb='Organization / Workspace'){
 const nav=[['Overview','overview','◫'],['Products','products','▦'],['Teams','teams','♧'],['Agents','agent-list','✦'],['Packs','packs','▧'],['Findings','change-inbox','⚑'],['PR Checks','pr-inbox','⑂'],['Evidence','evidence-register','◈'],['Providers','ep-catalog','⌁'],['Docs','docs-screen','▤'],['Settings','workspace','⚙']];
 const current=state.screens.find(s=>s.id===index)?.name||index;
  const active= index==='workspace'?'Settings':index.startsWith('team')?'Teams':index.startsWith('product')?'Products':(['pack-connect','pack-activation','pack-detail','packs','impact'].includes(index))?'Packs':(['finding','remediation','resolution'].includes(index)||index.startsWith('change-'))?'Findings':index.startsWith('pr-')?'PR Checks':index.startsWith('agent-')?'Agents':index==='evidence-detail'||index==='evidence-register'?'Evidence':index==='providers'||index==='provider-detail'||index.startsWith('ep-')?'Providers':index==='docs-screen'?'Docs':index==='overview'?'Overview':'';
 return `<div class="portal"><div class="portal-sidebar"><div class="portal-logo"><span class="brandmark">◇</span> Specbound</div><div>${nav.map(([label,id,ic])=>`<button class="navitem ${active===label?'on':''}" data-go="${id}"><span class="navico">${ic}</span>${label}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="nav-spacer"></div><div class="sidebar-workspace"><div class="avatar">AC</div><div><b style="font-size:10px">Acme Engineering</b><div class="t-sub">Organization workspace</div></div><span style="margin-left:auto;color:#9badc2">⌄</span></div></div><div class="portal-main"><div class="portal-top"><span class="crumb">◈ &nbsp;Acme Engineering &nbsp;/&nbsp; <b>${esc(crumb)}</b></span><div class="top-search">⌕ &nbsp; Search products, packs, controls… <span style="margin-left:auto">⌘ K</span></div><span class="top-round">♧</span><div class="avatar" style="border-radius:50%;background:#e5f4ee;color:#119772">AM</div></div><main class="portal-body">${content}</main></div></div>`;
}
function overview(){let trend=`<svg class="trend-svg" viewBox="0 0 450 170" preserveAspectRatio="none"><g stroke="#e8eef6" stroke-width="1">${[25,60,95,130].map(y=>`<path d="M28 ${y}H443"/>`).join('')}</g><g font-size="10" fill="#a1aebf"><text x="3" y="29">900</text><text x="3" y="64">600</text><text x="3" y="99">300</text><text x="11" y="134">0</text><text x="28" y="160">Jan 1</text><text x="123" y="160">Jan 8</text><text x="218" y="160">Jan 15</text><text x="325" y="160">Jan 22</text><text x="407" y="160">Jan 29</text></g><path d="M28 83 C60 88 80 66 109 70 S157 51 183 58 S221 42 249 48 S300 31 330 38 S395 25 443 23" stroke="#21b88b" stroke-width="3.2" fill="none"/><path d="M28 116 Q85 105 110 111 T200 101 T300 106 T443 88" stroke="#e47b81" stroke-width="2.7" fill="none"/><path d="M28 136 Q90 138 135 130 T235 123 T330 120 T443 115" stroke="#edbd5b" stroke-width="2.7" fill="none"/></svg>`;
return shell('overview',`<div class="eyebrow">PORTFOLIO HEALTH</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>Overview</h1><p>Governance packs from Git, automatically assessed against your products.</p></div>${btn('↻ Refresh','refresh','')} </div><div class="dash-row stats">${stat('Active Packs','3','↑ 1')}${stat('Registered Products','12','↑ 2')}${stat('Controls Evaluated','1,248','↑ 6%')}${stat('Open Findings','37','↓ 12%',true)}${stat('Unknown Evidence','19','↓ 28%',true)}</div><div class="viz"><div class="panel"><div class="panelheader"><h3>Assessment trend</h3><span class="subtle">Last 30 days ⌄</span></div>${trend}<div class="legend" style="display:flex;gap:25px;justify-content:center"><div><i class="dot"></i> Pass</div><div><i class="dot red"></i> Fail</div><div><i class="dot amber"></i> Unknown</div></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="panelheader"><h3>Portfolio posture</h3><span class="subtle">Latest assessments</span></div><div class="donutrow"><div class="donut"><div><b>78%</b><span>Pass</span></div></div><div class="legend"><div><i class="dot"></i> Pass&nbsp;&nbsp;78%</div><div><i class="dot red"></i> Fail&nbsp;&nbsp;13%</div><div><i class="dot amber"></i> Unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;9%</div></div></div></div></div><div class="overview-bottom"><div class="panel"><h3>Most impacted products</h3>${row('<span class="link" data-go="product-detail">customer-service</span>',status('12 open','red'))}${row('billing-api',status('8 open','red'))}${row('consent-service',status('6 open','amber'))}${btn('Browse products →','products','small')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Active governance packs</h3>${row('◈ security-pack',status('Active','green'))}${row('◈ privacy-pack',status('Active','green'))}${row('◈ architecture-pack',status('Draft','amber'))}${btn('View packs →','packs','small')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Recent findings</h3>${row('<span class="link" data-go="finding">⚠ Database publicly reachable</span>','10m ago')}${row('⚠ Missing deletion evidence','24m ago')}${row('⚠ Elevated IAM permissions','1h ago')}${btn('Inspect findings →','finding','small')}</div></div>`);
}
function packs(){const rows=[['security-pack','Platform Security','acme/governance-security','v1.2.0','48','Active','2 min'],['privacy-pack','Data protection','acme/governance-privacy','v1.1.0','31','Active','5 min'],['architecture-pack','Architecture & reliability','acme/governance-architecture','v0.9.0','45','Draft','18 min']];return shell('packs',`<div class="eyebrow">GOVERNANCE / SOURCES</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>Governance Packs</h1><p>Versioned rules are read directly from approved Git repositories.</p></div>${btn('+ Connect repository','connect','blue')}</div><div class="filterbar"><button class="filter">All statuses ⌄</button><button class="filter">All owners ⌄</button><span class="filter" style="margin-left:auto">⌕ Search packs</span></div><div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>PACK</th><th>GIT REPOSITORY</th><th>RELEASE TAG</th><th>CONTROLS</th><th>STATUS</th><th>SYNC</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="pack-detail"><td><div style="display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:center"><span class="pack-icon">▧</span><div><b>${r[0]}</b><div class="t-sub">${r[1]}</div></div></div></td><td><span class="repo-link">◉ ${r[2]}</span></td><td><span class="code-chip">${r[3]}</span><div class="t-sub">Pinned at activation</div></td><td><b>${r[4]}</b></td><td>${status(r[5])}</td><td>${r[6]} ago</td><td><button class="pbutton small" data-go="pack-detail">View →</button></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`);}

function packDetail(){const tab=demo.tabs['pack-detail'];let main='';if(tab==='Controls')main=`<div class="controls-layout"><div class="table-card control-list"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>CONTROL</th><th>DESCRIPTION</th><th>SUBJECT</th><th>CAPABILITY</th><th>SEVERITY</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['SEC-NET-001','Restrict public DB access','Database','net.internet-reachability','High'],['SEC-STO-002','Encrypt storage at rest','Storage','storage.encryption','High'],['SEC-LOG-003','Audit logging enabled','Service','audit.log-configuration','Medium'],['SEC-IAM-004','Least privilege access','Principal','iam.permission-scope','Medium'],['SEC-DEP-005','No critical dependencies','Software','supplychain.vulnerability','High']].map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="finding"><td><span class="link">${r[0]}</span></td><td>${r[1]}</td><td>${r[2]}</td><td><span class="code-chip">${r[3]}</span></td><td>${status(r[4],r[4]==='High'?'red':'amber')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><div class="details-panel"><h3 style="margin-top:0">SEC-NET-001</h3><div class="caption" style="margin-bottom:16px">Database network access restriction · selected control</div><div class="detail-step"><b>Source</b><span>security-pack · release v1.2.0<br>policy.md · section 4.2</span></div><div class="detail-step"><b>Control</b><span>Database publicly reachable = false</span></div><div class="detail-step"><b>Required evidence</b><span>net.internet-reachability v1<br>verified provider · max 24h</span></div><div class="detail-step"><b>Assessment</b><span>PASS / FAIL / UNKNOWN / N/A</span></div>${btn('View related finding →','finding','small blue')}</div></div>`;
else if(tab==='Manifest')main=`<div class="spec-layout"><div class="panel"><h3>pack.yaml · governance pack</h3>${codeExample('apiVersion: specbound.example/v1alpha1\nkind: GovernancePack\nmetadata:\n  id: com.acme.security\n  version: 1.2.0\ncontrols:\n  - controls/SEC-NET-001.yaml\nrequiresCapabilities:\n  - net.internet-reachability/v1')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>controls/SEC-NET-001.yaml</h3>${codeExample('id: SEC-NET-001\ntarget:\n  kind: database\nrequiredEvidence:\n  capability: net.internet-reachability/v1\nassertions:\n  - path: publicly_reachable\n    operator: equals\n    expected: false')}</div></div>`;
else if(tab==='Releases')main=card('Reviewed Git releases',row('<span class="code-chip">v1.2.0</span> · current approved release','2h ago')+row('<span class="code-chip">v1.1.0</span> · previous release','7d ago')+row('Tag target: a7c3f9e · kept in audit record','Pinned')+btn('Compare versions →','impact','small blue'));
else if(tab==='README')main=card('README.md · repository preview','<div class="app-demo-notice"><b>Corporate Security Pack</b><p>A versioned, reviewed collection of security controls and evidence contracts. Rules are maintained in Git independently of the Specbound runtime.</p><code>pack.yaml · controls/ · tests/ · docs/</code></div>');
else main=card('Pack overview','<div class="app-demo-notice">48 declarative controls · 5 evidence capabilities · 3 enabled environments. Source repository is authoritative. Approved releases are selected by tag and resolved to an exact commit for reproducible assessments.</div>');
return shell('pack-detail',`<div class="eyebrow">PACKS / SECURITY-PACK</div><div class="pagehead"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><span class="pack-icon" style="width:46px;height:46px;font-size:25px">⑂</span><div><h1>security-pack ${status('Active')}</h1><p>Corporate security controls · Git-managed · reviewed by Platform Governance</p></div></div><div class="h-actions">${btn('Simulate','impact')}${btn('Compare version →','impact','blue')}</div></div><div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr .8fr 1.4fr .8fr"><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">SOURCE REPOSITORY</div><div class="info-value">⑂ github.com/acme/governance-security-pack</div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">ACTIVE RELEASE</div><div class="info-value"><span class="code-chip" style="font-weight:800;color:#246fcb">v1.2.0</span></div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">RELEASE PROVENANCE</div><div class="info-value"><span style="color:#14926d">✓ Verified snapshot</span> <button class="audit-link" data-go="revision-details">Audit details ↗</button></div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">LAST SYNC</div><div class="info-value">2 min ago</div></div></div><div class="tabs">${['Overview','Controls','Manifest','Releases','README'].map(t=>`<button class="tab ${tab===t?'selected':''}" data-tab="${t}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>${main}`);
}
function impact(){const products=[['customer-service','Pass','Fail','−1'],['billing-api','Pass','Fail','−1'],['consent-service','Fail','Fail','—'],['web-portal','Pass','Pass','—'],['reporting-service','Pass','Pass','—'],['analytics-worker','Pass','Unknown','−1']];return shell('impact',`<div class="eyebrow">PACKS / SECURITY-PACK / SIMULATE</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>Impact Analysis ${status('Simulated','blue')}</h1><p>Preview the outcome of a candidate Git release tag before activating it.</p></div>${btn('← Pack details','pack-detail')}</div><div class="timeline-versions"><div class="version-box"><span class="muted">CURRENT · ACTIVE REVISION</span><b>v1.1.0</b><span class="muted">Approved · 7 days ago</span></div><span style="text-align:center;font-size:22px;color:#8aa5c1">→</span><div class="version-box next"><span class="muted">CANDIDATE · FROM GIT</span><b>v1.2.0</b><span class="muted">Candidate · 2 hours ago</span></div>${status('+8 controls', 'blue')}</div><div class="dash-row stats" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin-bottom:13px">${stat('Impacted products','6','review')}${stat('New failing checks','+8','↑ risk',true)}${stat('Changed controls','4','modified')}${stat('Missing evidence','+3','unknown',true)}</div><div class="outcome-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="panelheader"><h3>Predicted outcomes by product</h3><span class="subtle">6 affected products</span></div><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>PRODUCT</th><th>CURRENT</th><th>PREDICTED</th><th>Δ</th></tr></thead><tbody>${products.map(p=>`<tr><td><b>${p[0]}</b></td><td>${status(p[1])}</td><td>${status(p[2])}</td><td style="color:${p[3]==='—'?'#a0aebe':'#ce6c6c'}">${p[3]}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><div class="panel"><h3>Activation plan</h3>${[['simulate','Simulate only','Evaluate without changing enforcement'],['gradual','Gradual rollout','Selected products, then expand'],['enforce','Enforce all','Apply to all applicable products']].map(x=>`<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="rollout" value="${x[0]}" ${demo.scope===x[0]||(demo.scope==='all'&&x[0]==='simulate')?'checked':''}><span><b>${x[1]}</b><small>${x[2]}</small></span></label>`).join('')}<button class="pbutton blue" style="width:100%;margin-top:7px" data-go="simulate">${demo.simulated?'✓ Simulation complete':'▶ Run simulation'}</button><div style="font-size:10px;color:#8798ad;margin-top:13px">${demo.simulated?'Preview created locally from illustrative sample data. No policy evaluation was executed.':'No changes are applied until a separately approved activation.'}</div></div></div>`);
}
function products(){let rows=[['customer-service','Service','Prod','Python · AWS','3 / 3','Fail','5 min','12'],['billing-api','API','Prod','TypeScript · PostgreSQL','3 / 3','Fail','8 min','8'],['consent-service','Service','Staging','Python · Kubernetes','3 / 3','Fail','12 min','6'],['web-portal','Web App','Prod','TypeScript · AWS','2 / 3','Pass','10 min','0'],['reporting-service','Service','Prod','Go · AWS','3 / 3','Pass','20 min','0'],['analytics-worker','Worker','Staging','Python · ECS','2 / 3','Unknown','18 min','3']];if(demo.filter!=='all')rows=rows.filter(r=>demo.filter==='production'?r[2]==='Prod':r[5]===demo.filter);if(demo.search)rows=rows.filter(r=>r.join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(demo.search.toLowerCase()));return shell('products',`<div class="eyebrow">PRODUCTS / INVENTORY</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>Products</h1><p>Discovered applications, infrastructure, and evidence coverage.</p></div>${btn('+ Register product','product-create','blue')}</div><div class="filterbar"><div class="filter">Environment <select data-filter="environment"><option value="all">All</option><option value="production" ${demo.filter==='production'?'selected':''}>Production</option><option value="Fail" ${demo.filter==='Fail'?'selected':''}>Failing</option><option value="Unknown" ${demo.filter==='Unknown'?'selected':''}>Unknown</option></select></div><button class="filter">Team: All ⌄</button><button class="filter">Technology: All ⌄</button><label class="filter" style="margin-left:auto">⌕ <input class="txtinput" placeholder="Search products…" value="${esc(demo.search)}" data-search></label></div><div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>PRODUCT</th><th>TYPE</th><th>ENV</th><th>TECHNOLOGIES</th><th>PACK COVERAGE</th><th>POSTURE</th><th>ASSESSED</th><th>FINDINGS</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="product-detail"><td><b>◇ ${r[0]}</b></td><td>${r[1]}</td><td>${status(r[2],r[2]==='Prod'?'green':'blue')}</td><td>${r[3]}</td><td><span class="code-chip">${r[4]}</span></td><td>${status(r[5])}</td><td>${r[6]} ago</td><td>${status(r[7],+r[7]?'red':'green')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:16px">${card('Discovery sources',row('Git repositories',status('Connected','green'))+row('AWS resources',status('Connected','green'))+row('OpenAPI specs',status('Connected','green')))}${card('Coverage quality',row('Registered products','12')+row('Fully mapped to controls','9 / 12')+row('Unknown relationships',status('3 gaps','amber')))}</div>`);
}
function architecture(){return `<div class="architecture"><svg class="arch-lines" viewBox="0 0 520 313" preserveAspectRatio="none"><g fill="none" stroke="#95b8dd" stroke-width="2"><path d="M259 84V107H140V135"/><path d="M259 107H381V135"/><path d="M140 187V222H141V246"/><path d="M381 187V222H375V246"/><path d="M140 222H381"/></g></svg><div class="node" style="left:185px;top:25px;min-width:150px;border-color:#9fc5f9;background:#f2f8ff"><span class="nicon">◇</span><div><b>customer-service</b><small>Python / FastAPI</small></div></div><div class="node" style="left:55px;top:135px"><span class="nicon">↗</span><div><b>REST API</b><small>HTTPS · 443</small></div></div><div class="node" style="left:317px;top:135px"><span class="nicon">⚙</span><div><b>Worker</b><small>Background jobs</small></div></div><div class="node" style="left:66px;top:246px"><span class="nicon">▤</span><div><b>PostgreSQL</b><small>db-primary</small></div></div><div class="node" style="left:319px;top:246px"><span class="nicon">▣</span><div><b>S3 Bucket</b><small>Artifacts</small></div></div></div>`}
function productDetail(){const tab=demo.tabs['product-detail'];let content=tab==='Controls'?`<div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>CONTROL</th><th>PACK</th><th>RESOURCE</th><th>STATUS</th><th>EVIDENCE</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['SEC-NET-001','security-pack','db-primary','Fail','AWS network provider'],['SEC-STO-002','security-pack','PostgreSQL','Pass','AWS Config'],['PRI-DAT-003','privacy-pack','customer-email','Unknown','Missing test'],['ARCH-API-003','architecture-pack','REST API','Pass','OpenAPI Provider']].map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="finding">${r.map((c,i)=>`<td>${i===3?status(c):c}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`:tab==='Evidence'?card('Evidence provenance',row('net.internet-reachability','AWS provider · observed 5m ago')+row('storage.encryption','AWS Config · observed 5m ago')+row('data.retention','UNKNOWN · not provided')):tab==='History'?card('Assessment history',row('Current revision · 9d2e8f1',status('Fail'))+row('Previous revision · 73da5c2',status('Pass'))):`<div class="product-layout"><div class="panel"><h3>Architecture · inferred product twin</h3>${architecture()}</div><div><div class="panel"><h3>Applicable controls (from Packs)</h3>${row('<span class="link" data-go="pack-detail">security-pack</span> · v1.2.0',status('Fail'))}${row('privacy-pack · v1.1.0',status('Unknown'))}${row('architecture-pack · v0.9.0',status('Pass'))}${btn('View failed control →','finding','small blue')}</div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:11px"><h3>Evidence summary</h3><div class="evidence-metrics"><div class="metric"><b>41</b><small>Collected</small></div><div class="metric"><b style="color:#15a477">35</b><small>Pass</small></div><div class="metric"><b style="color:#df6869">4</b><small>Fail</small></div><div class="metric"><b style="color:#d29a3e">2</b><small>Unknown</small></div></div></div></div></div>`;
return shell('product-detail',`<div class="eyebrow">PRODUCTS / CUSTOMER-SERVICE</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>◇ customer-service ${status('Active','green')}</h1><p>Customer management backend · Production · Customer Platform Team</p></div>${btn('↻ Reassess','reassess','blue')}</div><div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr 1.5fr"><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">TYPE</div><div class="info-value">Backend Service</div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">ENVIRONMENT</div><div class="info-value">Production</div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">TEAM</div><div class="info-value">Customer Platform</div></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">TECHNOLOGY</div><div class="info-value">Python · AWS · PostgreSQL</div></div></div><div class="tabs">${['Components','Controls','Evidence','History'].map(t=>`<button class="tab ${demo.tabs['product-detail']===t?'selected':''}" data-tab="${t}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>${content}`);
}
function finding(){let chain=[['Requirement','Network access restricted'],['Control','SEC-NET-001'],['Capability','net.internet-reachability'],['Provider','AWS network'],['Observation','public = true'],['Assessment','FAIL']];const tabs=['Details','Evidence','Timeline'];let tab=demo.tabs['finding'];if(!tabs.includes(tab))tab='Details';let body=tab==='Details'?`<div class="finding-layout"><div><div class="panel"><h3>Traceability & Assessment</h3><div class="chain">${chain.map((c,i)=>`${i?'<span class="arr">›</span>':''}<div class="chain-step" ${i===5?'style="background:#fff2f2;border-color:#ffd2d2"':''}><b>${c[0]}</b><small>${c[1]}</small></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="divider"></div><h3>Observed data</h3><div class="kv"><span class="key">Resource</span><b>db-primary · PostgreSQL</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Publicly reachable</span><b style="color:#ca575b">true · 0.0.0.0/0</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Evidence source</span><b>AWS network provider</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Observed at</span><b>2026-11-01 18:24 UTC</b></div></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>Suggested remediation</h3>${[['Restrict database access to trusted private networks.'],['Update infrastructure code and open a normal Git pull request.'],['Allow the platform to automatically reassess the new revision.']].map((r,i)=>`<div class="guide-step"><span class="num">${i+1}</span><span>${r}</span></div>`).join('')}${btn('See resolution journey →','resolution','small blue')}</div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Related code / activity</h3><div class="subtle" style="margin-bottom:10px">RECENT COMMITS</div>${row('<span class="code-chip">a7c3f9e</span>','10m')}${row('<span class="code-chip">f12b4c8</span>','1d')}<div class="divider"></div><div class="subtle" style="margin-bottom:10px">PULL REQUESTS</div>${row('<span class="link" data-go="resolution">#482 Restrict RDS exposure</span>',status('Merged','green'))}${row('#476 Harden database access',status('Merged','green'))}<div class="divider"></div><div class="subtle">SOURCE PACK</div><p class="caption">security-pack · v1.2.0<br>SHA a7c3f9e · control SEC-NET-001</p>${btn('Open Pack →','pack-detail','small')}</div></div>`:tab==='Evidence'?card('Provider evidence',`<div class="kv"><span class="key">Capability</span><b>net.internet-reachability/v1</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Provider</span><b>AWS network provider</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Trust</span><b>verified provider</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Max age</span><b>PT24H</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Observation</span><b style="color:#ca575b">publicly_reachable: true</b></div><div class="kv"><span class="key">Evidence digest</span><b>sha256:8f7b…91ac</b></div>`):card('Finding timeline',row('2026-11-01 · 18:24','Evidence collected')+row('2026-11-01 · 18:25','Control evaluated: FAIL')+row('2026-11-01 · 18:26','Pull request #482 linked'));
return shell('finding',`<div class="eyebrow">FINDINGS / FND-7621</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>⚠ Database is publicly reachable</h1><p>Observed network reachability conflicts with SEC-NET-001.</p></div>${status('Fail','red')}</div><div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:.75fr 1.2fr 1.3fr 1fr 1fr"><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">SEVERITY</div>${status('High','red')}</div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">PRODUCT</div><b class="link" data-go="product-detail">customer-service</b></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">RESOURCE</div><b>db-primary</b></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">CONTROL</div><b>SEC-NET-001</b></div><div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">PACK</div><b class="link" data-go="pack-detail">security-pack</b></div></div><div class="tabs">${tabs.map(t=>`<button class="tab ${tab===t?'selected':''}" data-tab="${t}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>${body}`);
}
function resolution(){return shell('resolution',`<div class="eyebrow">PRODUCTS / CUSTOMER-SERVICE / RESOLUTION</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>✓ Resolution Loop</h1><p>From detected finding to code change and automatic reassessment.</p></div>${status('Resolved','green')}</div><div class="panel"><div class="resolution-flow">${[['Finding detected','18:24'],['Code change (PR)','19:05'],['Reassessment','19:08'],['Resolved','19:08']].map(r=>`<div class="res-step"><span class="res-tick">✓</span><b>${r[0]}</b><small>Nov 1 · ${r[1]}</small></div>`).join('')}</div></div><div class="resolved-columns" style="margin-top:13px"><div class="panel"><div class="panelheader"><h3>Git pull request</h3>${status('Merged','green')}</div><div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:11px"><span class="pack-icon">⑂</span><div><b class="link">#482 Restrict database ingress to private networks</b><p class="caption">Terraform updated: removed public network ingress and verified private connectivity.</p></div></div><div class="divider"></div>${row('Author','@dev-alex')}${row('Merged revision','<span class="code-chip">9d2e8f1</span>')}${row('Trigger','Git webhook → platform reassessment')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Assessment result · after fix</h3>${row('security-pack · v1.2.0',status('Pass','green'))}${row('privacy-pack · v1.1.0',status('Pass','green'))}${row('architecture-pack · v0.9.0',status('Pass','green'))}<div class="app-demo-notice" style="margin-top:10px"><b>All applicable sample controls pass.</b><br>Same Git packs, updated verified provider observation.</div></div></div><div class="resolved-columns" style="margin-top:13px;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr"><div class="panel"><h3>Before / after</h3><div class="before-after"><div class="compare"><b style="color:#c54b4f">FAIL</b><small>Database public<br>SEC-NET-001</small></div><div style="text-align:center;font-size:20px;color:#94aac2">→</div><div class="compare after"><b style="color:#10936b">PASS</b><small>Database private<br>SEC-NET-001</small></div></div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Closed-loop contract</h3><p class="caption">A human developer or AI agent fixes the ordinary Git repository. The platform detects the change, collects new evidence and updates the assessment automatically. No dedicated CLI in product teams.</p>${btn('Return to overview →','overview','small blue')}</div></div>`);
}
function docsPage(){const tab=demo.docsTab||'Start';let body=tab==='Start'?`<div class="docs-grid"><div class="panel docs-hero"><span class="docs-icon">◎</span><h2>Understand the Specbound</h2><p>Explore the open platform: connect Git-managed governance packs, assess software products automatically and trace every outcome to evidence.</p>${btn('Explore governance packs →','docs-packs','blue')}${btn('Evidence Provider Packs →','ep-manifest','small')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Popular guides</h3>${row('<span class="link" data-go="docs-packs">Governance Packs & releases</span>','↗')}${row('<span class="link" data-go="docs-evidence">Evidence & assessments</span>','↗')}${row('<span class="link" data-go="docs-connect">Connecting your systems</span>','↗')}${row('<span class="link" data-go="ep-manifest">Provider manifest example</span>','↗')}${row('<span class="link" data-go="agent-list">AI agent identities</span>','↗')}</div></div><div class="docs-tiles">${[['01','Connect source repositories','Admin registers a Git repository. The portal reads validated pack definitions at a pinned release.'],['02','Assess products','Providers observe products and produce typed, timestamped evidence.'],['03','Explain every finding','Controls and observations are traceable, including unknown or missing evidence.']].map(([n,t,d])=>`<div class="panel"><div class="docs-step">${n}</div><h3>${t}</h3><p class="caption">${d}</p></div>`).join('')}</div>`:tab==='Packs'?`<div class="docs-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Packs live in Git</h3><p class="caption">A pack contains a versioned manifest, controls, capability contracts and test cases. Authors may be humans or AI agents; the portal only consumes validated, reviewed releases.</p><div class="docs-code">governance-pack/<br>├── pack.yaml<br>├── controls/<br>├── tests/<br>└── docs/</div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Release integrity</h3>${row('Human-readable release','<span class="code-chip">v1.2.0</span>')}${row('Immutable content reference','<span class="code-chip">Git commit SHA</span>')}${row('Recommended repository policy',status('Protected tags','green'))}<p class="caption">Tags can be moved unless protected. On activation the platform resolves a tag to a specific commit and stores it in the audit record. Signed tags and immutable releases add provenance protection.</p>${btn('Open Pack Details →','pack-detail','small blue')}</div></div>`:tab==='Evidence'?`<div class="panel"><h3>Evidence-driven assessment</h3><p class="caption">A provider collects facts from repositories, cloud configuration and test environments. Packs describe the required capability; the core evaluates independent checks. Missing evidence does not silently pass.</p><div class="chain">${[['Requirement','what is needed'],['Control','testable goal'],['Capability','evidence type'],['Provider','observation'],['Assessment','pass / fail / unknown']].map((c,i)=>`${i?'<span class="arr">›</span>':''}<div class="chain-step"><b>${c[0]}</b><small>${c[1]}</small></div>`).join('')}</div>${btn('Open example finding →','finding','small blue')}</div>`:`<div class="docs-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Connect the platform</h3><p class="caption">Connect source repositories and product environments once at the organization level. Product teams do not need a Governance CLI or a language-specific SDK for standard scans.</p>${row('Git providers','Repository discovery & PR checks')}${row('Cloud providers','Observed infrastructure state')}${row('OpenAPI and schemas','Service facts and contracts')}${btn('View products →','products','small blue')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Authoring is independent</h3><p class="caption">The platform neither uploads PDFs nor creates governance rules. A separate optional authoring skill may help a human or AI agent write, test and review a Git-based pack.</p><p class="caption">All data shown in this prototype is illustrative.</p></div></div>`;return shell('docs-screen',`<div class="eyebrow">LEARN / DOCUMENTATION</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>Documentation</h1><p>Learn the platform, its extension model and the governance-to-evidence lifecycle.</p></div>${btn('Browse Packs →','packs')}</div><div class="tabs docs-tabs">${['Start','Packs','Evidence','Integrations'].map(t=>`<button class="tab ${tab===t?'selected':''}" data-doc-tab="${t}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>${body}`)}


/* Additional journeys: Team, Product, Governance, Evidence, Operations */
const progress=(labels,active)=>`<div class="wizard-progress">${labels.map((x,i)=>`<div class="wizard-step ${i<active?'done':i===active?'current':''}"><span>${i<active?'✓':i+1}</span><b>${x}</b></div>`).join('<span class="wizard-chevron">›</span>')}</div>`;
const field=(label,value,placeholder,id,help='')=>`<label class="app-label">${label}<input class="app-input" data-demo-input="${id}" value="${esc(value)}" placeholder="${esc(placeholder||'')}" /></label>${help?`<div class="app-help">${help}</div>`:''}`;
const selectField=(label,options,selected,id)=>`<label class="app-label">${label}<select class="app-input" data-demo-input="${id}">${options.map(v=>`<option value="${esc(v)}" ${v===selected?'selected':''}>${esc(v)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label>`;
const infoTag=(title,value)=>`<div class="info-cell"><div class="info-label">${title}</div><div class="info-value">${value}</div></div>`;
const nextCard=(title,text,go,label='Continue →')=>`<div class="nextcard"><div><h3>${title}</h3><p>${text}</p></div>${btn(label,go,'blue')}</div>`;
const topTitle=(eyebrow,title,description,actions='')=>`<div class="eyebrow">${eyebrow}</div><div class="pagehead"><div><h1>${title}</h1><p>${description}</p></div><div class="h-actions">${actions}</div></div>`;
const backNext=(back,next,text='Continue →')=>`<div class="form-actions">${btn('← Back',back)}${btn(text,next,'blue')}</div>`;
function workspace(){return shell('workspace',`${topTitle('ORGANIZATION / SETTINGS','Workspace settings','Organization identity, team ownership and governed system connections.',btn('Manage teams →','teams','blue'))}<div class="setting-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Acme Engineering</h3><div class="orglogo">AC</div>${row('Workspace ID','acme-engineering')}${row('Identity provider',status('Connected','green'))}${row('Organization admins','3 accounts')}${row('Audit retention','365 days')}${btn('View teams →','teams','small blue')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Identity & access</h3>${row('Single sign-on','OIDC / SAML')}${row('Provisioning','SCIM enabled')}${row('Team roles','Admin · Maintainer · Viewer')}${row('Products require owner',status('Enforced','green'))}<div class="app-demo-notice">Teams are logical ownership boundaries. They are not automatically derived from Git organizations.</div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Platform connections</h3>${row('GitHub organization',status('Connected','green'))}${row('AWS account federation',status('Connected','green'))}${row('GitLab provider',status('Not set','amber'))}<p class="caption">Only organization admins connect privileged infrastructure. Product teams do not install a CLI.</p></div></div>${nextCard('First create an owning team','Products are always assigned to a team. Team membership and organization-wide integrations are managed separately.','teams','Open team directory →')}`,'Settings / Workspace')}
function teams(){const result=`<div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>TEAM</th><th>TEAM ADMIN</th><th>MEMBERS</th><th>PRODUCTS</th><th>STATUS</th><th>LAST CHANGE</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="clickable" data-go="team-detail"><td><b>Customer Platform</b><div class="t-sub">customer-platform</div></td><td>Lea Richter</td><td>7</td><td>3</td><td>${status('Active','green')}</td><td>Today</td></tr><tr><td><b>Billing Systems</b><div class="t-sub">billing-systems</div></td><td>Marco Weber</td><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>${status('Active','green')}</td><td>Yesterday</td></tr><tr><td><b>Architecture Enablement</b><div class="t-sub">architecture-enablement</div></td><td>Nina Hoffmann</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>${status('Active','green')}</td><td>4 days ago</td></tr></tbody></table></div>`;return shell('teams',`${topTitle('ORGANIZATION / PEOPLE','Teams','Assign clear responsibility for products, findings and evidence.',btn('+ Create team','team-create','blue'))}<div class="dash-row stats" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin-bottom:17px">${stat('Registered Teams','8','')}${stat('Team Members','54','')}${stat('Owned Products','12','')}${stat('Products without owner','0','—')}</div><div class="filterbar"><div class="filter">All teams ⌄</div><div class="filter">Status: Active ⌄</div><div class="filter">⌕ Search teams</div></div>${result}<div class="help-inline"><b>Human + agent members</b> · Teams can contain people and individually identified AI agents. An agent may join multiple teams, but every action is attributed to its own account and limited to explicit scopes. <span class="link" data-go="agent-list">Manage agents →</span></div>${nextCard('Create the Customer Platform team','The wizard captures team identity, a responsible owner and its initial members.','team-create','Create team →')}`,'Organization / Teams')}
function teamCreate(){return shell('team-create',`${topTitle('TEAMS / NEW TEAM','Create team','Step 1 of 3 — Choose the team identity and its accountable owner.')}${progress(['Team details','Members & roles','Review ownership'],0)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Basic details</h3>${field('Team name',demo.teamName,'e.g. Customer Platform','teamName','Visible in products, findings and organization reports.')}${field('Team identifier',demo.teamSlug,'e.g. customer-platform','teamSlug','Stable ID for references; changing it later requires explicit migration.')}<label class="app-label">Description<textarea class="app-input" data-demo-input="teamDescription" rows="3">${esc(demo.teamDescription)}</textarea></label>${selectField('Team admin (organization member)',['Lea Richter','Nina Hoffmann','Marco Weber'],'Lea Richter','teamAdmin')}</div><div class="panel side-hint"><h3>Team responsibilities</h3><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">1</span><div><b>Own products</b><p>Every registered product has exactly one responsible team.</p></div></div><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">2</span><div><b>Receive findings</b><p>Findings are routed to the product's owning team.</p></div></div><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">3</span><div><b>Manage access</b><p>Team admins maintain membership; organization admins control platform connections.</p></div></div><div class="app-demo-notice">No Git repository or SDK is required to create a team.</div></div></div>${backNext('teams','team-members')}`,'Teams / Create team')}
function teamMembers(){const userRows=[['Lea Richter','lea.richter@acme.example','Team Admin','Owner'],['Jonas Berg','jonas.berg@acme.example','Maintainer','Existing user'],['Mira Albrecht','mira.albrecht@acme.example','Viewer','Existing user'],['Customer Fix Agent','agent/customer-fix','Agent · PR proposer','Service identity']];return shell('team-members',`${topTitle('TEAMS / NEW TEAM','Add members & roles','Step 2 of 3 — Grant team access without exposing organization-wide credentials.')}${progress(['Team details','Members & roles','Review ownership'],1)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Team membership</h3><div class="team-user-list">${userRows.map(([n,email,role,note])=>`<div class="team-user"><span class="person">${n.split(' ').map(x=>x[0]).join('')}</span><div class="grow"><b>${n}</b><small>${email}</small></div>${status(role,role==='Team Admin'?'blue':'')}<span class="t-sub">${note}</span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="inline-invite"><input class="app-input" data-demo-input="inviteEmail" placeholder="Invite by email or search directory…"><select class="app-input" data-demo-input="selectedRole"><option>Maintainer</option><option>Viewer</option><option>Team Admin</option></select>${btn('+ Add','invite-user','blue')}</div><p class="caption">Invitations are limited to approved organization identities. Additional users can be added after team creation.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Role definitions</h3>${row('<b>Team Admin</b>','Membership + product ownership')}${row('<b>Maintainer</b>','Register products + manage findings')}${row('<b>Viewer</b>','Read products, evidence and history')}<div class="app-demo-notice"><b>Separation of duties</b><br>Team roles do not authorize changes to governance packs or organization-wide evidence providers.</div>${row('<b>Agent · PR proposer</b>','Create PRs; cannot approve/merge')}${btn('Manage agent identities →','agent-list','small blue')}${btn('See role documentation →','docs-screen','small')}</div></div>${backNext('team-create','team-detail','Review team →')}`,'Teams / Members & roles')}
function teamDetail(){return shell('team-detail',`${topTitle('TEAMS / CUSTOMER PLATFORM',esc(demo.teamName), 'Team settings, members, responsibilities and owned products.',btn('+ Register product','product-create','blue'))}<div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">${infoTag('TEAM ID',esc(demo.teamSlug))}${infoTag('TEAM ADMIN','Lea Richter')}${infoTag('MEMBERS','3 assigned')}${infoTag('OWNED PRODUCTS','3 services')}</div><div class="team-dash"><div class="panel"><h3>Members & permissions</h3>${row('Lea Richter',status('Team Admin','blue'))}${row('Jonas Berg',status('Maintainer',''))}${row('Mira Albrecht',status('Viewer',''))}${row('✦ Customer Fix Agent',status('Agent · PR proposer','blue'))}${btn('Manage agent →','agent-list','small blue')}${btn('Edit membership →','team-members','small')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Owned products</h3>${row('<span class="link" data-go="product-detail">customer-service</span>',status('12 findings','red'))}${row('customer-events',status('Pass','green'))}${row('customer-portal',status('Unknown','amber'))}${btn('Open product inventory →','products','small')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Assignments & notifications</h3>${row('Finding routing','Owning team')}${row('Escalation contact','Lea Richter')}${row('Assessment digest','Weekly')}${row('Default environment','Production')}${btn('View organization →','workspace','small')}</div></div>${nextCard('Now register a product','Use this team as the accountable product owner. Next, connect the repository and discover its components.','product-create','Register first product →')}`,'Teams / Customer Platform')}
function productCreate(){return shell('product-create',`${topTitle('PRODUCTS / REGISTER','Register a product','Step 1 of 3 — Define a stable product identity and accountable owning team.')}${progress(['Product identity','Connect sources','Review discovery'],0)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Product identity</h3>${field('Product name',demo.productName,'customer-service','productName','A unique and stable identifier for assessments and findings.')}${selectField('Product type',['Backend service','REST API','Web application','Batch processor'],demo.productType,'productType')}${selectField('Owning team',['Customer Platform','Billing Systems','Architecture Enablement'],demo.ownerTeam,'ownerTeam')}${selectField('Environment',['Production','Staging','Development'],'Production','environment')}<div class="help-inline">Product lifecycle and team lifecycle are independent. Ownership can later be transferred with an audit trail.</div></div><div class="panel side-hint"><h3>What happens next?</h3><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">1</span><div><b>Connect Git</b><p>Read-only access to the selected repository. No project file or CLI needs to be installed.</p></div></div><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">2</span><div><b>Discover components</b><p>Inspect OpenAPI, IaC and available cloud sources through organization connectors.</p></div></div><div class="hint-line"><span class="hint-mark">3</span><div><b>Assess with Packs</b><p>Applicable controls are selected centrally; unknown attributes remain explicit.</p></div></div></div></div>${backNext('products','product-repository','Connect sources →')}`,'Products / Register')}
function productRepository(){return shell('product-repository',`${topTitle('PRODUCTS / CONNECT SOURCES','Connect product sources','Step 2 of 3 — Connect Git and the runtime resources that belong to this product.')}${progress(['Product identity','Connect sources','Review discovery'],1)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Source repository ${status('Connected','green')}</h3>${selectField('Git integration',['GitHub · Acme Engineering','GitLab · Not configured'],'GitHub · Acme Engineering','gitIntegration')}${field('Repository',demo.repo,'acme/customer-service','repo','Only selected repositories are scanned by the organization integration.')}${selectField('Default release context',['main (development context)','Latest release tag'],'main (development context)','releaseContext')}<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Environment mapping</h3>${row('Production · AWS account','acme-prod / eu-central-1')}${row('Deployment workload','customer-service-prod')}${row('Cloud ownership matching',status('Suggested','blue'))}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Access boundaries</h3>${row('Repository scope','Read-only')}${row('Webhook triggers','PR · push · release')}${row('Cloud credentials','Organization connector')}${row('Secrets copied into product',status('None','green'))}<div class="app-demo-notice"><b>Without a CLI</b><br>Repository and cloud integrations run centrally. Team members only approve the scope they are allowed to connect.</div>${btn('How integrations work →','docs-screen','small')}</div></div>${backNext('product-create','product-discovery','Run discovery →')}`,'Products / Sources')}
function productDiscovery(){let items=[['◫','Backend service','customer-service','Git / Python project','Confirmed'],['⌁','REST API','/v1/customers','OpenAPI / routes','Confirmed'],['▤','PostgreSQL','db-primary','AWS configuration','Confirmed'],['▱','S3 bucket','customer-artifacts','Terraform / AWS','Confirmed']];return shell('product-discovery',`${topTitle('PRODUCTS / DISCOVERY','Review discovered components','Step 3 of 3 — Verify inferred facts, gaps and the boundary of this product.',status('Discovery complete','green'))}${progress(['Product identity','Connect sources','Review discovery'],2)}<div class="form-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1.22fr .78fr"><div class="panel"><h3>Automatically discovered inventory <span class="subtle">· illustrative</span></h3><div class="discover-list">${items.map(([icon,kind,name,src,st])=>`<div class="discover-row"><span class="discover-icon">${icon}</span><div><b>${name}</b><small>${kind} · ${src}</small></div>${status(st,'green')}</div>`).join('')}</div><p class="caption">Source provenance is retained for every fact. Uncertain ownership requires explicit review.</p></div><div><div class="panel"><h3>Missing product context</h3>${row('Processing purpose',status('Needs input','amber'))}${row('Retention policy',status('Unknown','amber'))}${row('API contract',status('Detected','green'))}${row('Infrastructure resources',status('Detected','green'))}<div class="app-demo-notice">Unknown is not Pass and is not automatically Not Applicable. The platform will request missing facts when they affect controls.</div></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:11px"><h3>Applicable pack selection</h3>${row('security-pack · v1.2.0',status('Applicable','blue'))}${row('privacy-pack · v1.1.0',status('Applicable','blue'))}${row('architecture-pack · v0.9.0',status('Applicable','blue'))}</div></div></div>${backNext('product-repository','product-detail','Register & view product →')}`,'Products / Discovery')}
function packConnect(){return shell('pack-connect',`${topTitle('PACKS / CONNECT REPOSITORY','Connect a Governance Pack','Connect a Git repository and select the reviewed release to be simulated or activated.')}${progress(['Repository','Select release','Evaluate impact'],1)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Pack source</h3>${selectField('Provider',['GitHub · Acme Engineering','GitLab · Not configured'],'GitHub · Acme Engineering','packProvider')}${field('Repository',demo.packRepo,'acme/governance-security','packRepo')}${selectField('Release tag',['v1.2.0','v1.1.0','v1.0.0'],demo.packTag,'packTag')}<div class="help-inline">For published releases, choose a tag. The platform resolves it to an exact commit and stores the pinned hash in the audit record.</div>${row('pack.yaml',status('Validated','green'))}${row('Control test cases',status('48 passed','green'))}${row('Required capability contracts',status('5 available','green'))}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Release integrity</h3>${row('Visible release','v1.2.0')}${row('Resolved content','a7c3f9e…')}${row('Tag protection',status('Enabled','green'))}${row('Signer identity',status('Verified','green'))}<div class="app-demo-notice">A tag can move unless constrained by repository policy. Re-resolving a changed tag must raise an integrity finding, never silently replace the approved revision.</div><h3 style="margin-top:18px">Flexible adoption</h3><p class="caption">Development and simulation can accept explicit commits. Organizations may require protected signed tags for production enforcement.</p></div></div>${backNext('packs','pack-detail','Inspect pack →')}`,'Packs / Connect repository')}
function packActivation(){return shell('pack-activation',`${topTitle('PACKS / SECURITY-PACK','Activate pack','Publish an approved governance release to selected product scopes.',status('Ready','green'))}${progress(['Repository','Select release','Evaluate impact'],2)}<div class="form-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Activation scope</h3>${row('Pack','security-pack · v1.2.0')}${row('Pinned revision','a7c3f9e…')}${row('Control definitions','48 validated')}${row('Organization','Acme Engineering')}${selectField('Environment scope',['Production only','All environments','Staging only'],'Production only','activationScope')}${selectField('Enforcement',['Monitor first','Block new releases','Audit only'],'Monitor first','enforcement')}<div class="app-demo-notice">Simulations do not change enforcement. Changes to active governance require an approval event.</div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Decision before activation</h3>${row('Impacted products','6')}${row('New failed assessments',status('8 predicted','red'))}${row('Missing evidence',status('3 unknown','amber'))}${row('Approval','Awaiting governance owner')}${btn('Review simulation →','impact','small')}<div class="approval-card"><b>Approval required</b><p>Owner: Platform Governance<br>Release tag: v1.2.0<br>Provenance: signed & pinned</p></div></div></div>${backNext('impact','packs','Preview activation →')}`,'Packs / Activation')}
function evidenceDetail(){const data=[['Evidence ID','evi-2026-0172'],['Capability','net.internet-reachability/v1'],['Subject','db-primary / customer-service'],['Observation','publicly_reachable = true'],['Produced by','AWS Network Provider 1.4.2'],['Observed','2026-11-02 · 07:43 UTC'],['Valid until','2026-11-03 · 07:43 UTC'],['Integrity','sha256:09ae…881c']];return shell('evidence-detail',`${topTitle('EVIDENCE / EVI-2026-0172','Evidence details','A typed observation with source attribution, scope, trust and freshness.',btn('View finding →','finding','blue'))}<div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">${infoTag('STATUS',status('Verified','green'))}${infoTag('TYPE','Cloud configuration')}${infoTag('FRESHNESS','Fresh · 24h TTL')}${infoTag('TRUST','Verified provider')}</div><div class="form-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr"><div class="panel"><h3>Observed evidence</h3><div class="keyvalue">${data.map(([k,v])=>`<div><span>${k}</span><b>${esc(v)}</b></div>`).join('')}</div><h3 style="margin-top:20px">Observation payload</h3><pre class="codewindow">{
  "subject": "aws:rds:db-primary",
  "capability": "net.internet-reachability/v1",
  "observation": { "publicly_reachable": true },
  "provider": "aws-network@1.4.2"
}</pre></div><div class="panel"><h3>Traceability</h3><div class="details-panel" style="border:0;padding:0">${[['Control','SEC-NET-001'],['Capability','net.internet-reachability/v1'],['Provider','AWS Network Provider'],['Observation','Reachable from public networks'],['Assessment','FAIL']].map(([a,b])=>`<div class="detail-step"><b>${a}</b><span>${b}</span></div>`).join('')}</div>${btn('Remediation options →','remediation','small blue')}</div></div>`,'Evidence / Inspection')}
function remediation(){return shell('remediation',`${topTitle('FINDINGS / FND-7621','Plan remediation','A verified finding is assigned to the owning team; development stays in the normal Git workflow.',btn('Open resolution →','resolution','blue'))}<div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">${infoTag('OWNER','Customer Platform')}${infoTag('PRIORITY',status('High','red'))}${infoTag('CONTROL','SEC-NET-001')}${infoTag('ENVIRONMENT','Production')}</div><div class="form-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1.18fr .82fr"><div class="panel"><h3>Technical change · #482</h3><div class="app-demo-notice">Repository: <b>acme/customer-service</b><br>Pull request: <b>Restrict database ingress to private subnets</b></div><div class="code-diff"><div class="line-minus">− publicly_accessible = true</div><div class="line-plus">+ publicly_accessible = false</div><div class="line-minus">− cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]</div><div class="line-plus">+ cidr_blocks = ["10.42.0.0/16"]</div></div><h3 style="margin-top:19px">Automated verification plan</h3>${row('Reassess cloud network exposure','After deployment')}${row('Verify exact deployed artifact','Required')}${row('Close only when observation passes','Enforced')}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Who is responsible?</h3>${row('Owning team','Customer Platform')}${row('Team admin','Lea Richter')}${row('Developer / AI agent','Can propose PR')}${row('Governance owner','Policy remains unchanged')}<h3 style="margin-top:20px">Finding timeline</h3>${row('Evidence observed','07:43 UTC')}${row('Finding created','07:45 UTC')}${row('PR opened','08:06 UTC')}${row('Deployment check','Pending')}${btn('See source evidence →','evidence-detail','small')}</div></div>${nextCard('Close the loop with an independent check','The platform compares new evidence to the pinned control version after deployment. A PR alone does not prove remediation.','resolution','Review resolution →')}`,'Findings / Remediation')}
function providers(){return shell('providers',`${topTitle('PLATFORM / PROVIDERS','Evidence Providers','Technical evidence collection is independent of governance controls.',btn('+ Connect provider','provider-detail','blue'))}<div class="dash-row stats" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin-bottom:14px">${stat('Connected providers','6','')}${stat('Capabilities','24','')}${stat('Healthy','5','')}${stat('Degraded','1','',true)}</div><div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>PROVIDER</th><th>TECHNOLOGY</th><th>CAPABILITIES</th><th>PRODUCTS</th><th>HEALTH</th><th>LAST CHECK</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['AWS Network Provider','AWS','net.internet-reachability · 4 more','8','Healthy'],['Git Repository Provider','GitHub','repo.dependencies · git.revision','12','Healthy'],['OpenAPI Provider','REST / OpenAPI','api.endpoints · auth.schema','7','Healthy'],['Kubernetes Provider','K8s','workload.security · network.policies','4','Degraded']].map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="provider-detail"><td><b>${r[0]}</b></td><td>${r[1]}</td><td>${r[2]}</td><td>${r[3]}</td><td>${status(r[4],r[4]==='Healthy'?'green':'amber')}</td><td>5 min ago</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>${nextCard('Inspect a capability provider','Providers observe products and produce signed or verified evidence. Packs consume the capability contract, not provider-specific implementations.','provider-detail','Inspect provider →')}`,'Providers / Directory')}
function providerDetail(){return shell('provider-detail',`${topTitle('PROVIDERS / AWS NETWORK','AWS Network Provider','Cloud configuration evidence without product-side SDKs or CLIs.',status('Healthy','green'))}<div class="git-info" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">${infoTag('VERSION','1.4.2')}${infoTag('INTEGRATION','AWS organization connector')}${infoTag('LAST SUCCESS','5 min ago')}${infoTag('TRUST','Verified provider')}</div><div class="form-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr"><div class="panel"><h3>Provided capabilities</h3>${row('<span class="code-chip">net.internet-reachability/v1</span>',status('Available','green'))}${row('<span class="code-chip">storage.encryption/v1</span>',status('Available','green'))}${row('<span class="code-chip">network.security-groups/v1</span>',status('Available','green'))}${row('<span class="code-chip">cloud.resource-identity/v1</span>',status('Available','green'))}<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Trust & collection</h3>${row('Authentication','Organization-scoped role')}${row('Permissions','Read-only, least privilege')}${row('Maximum age','24 hours')}${row('Provider self-test',status('Pass','green'))}</div><div class="panel"><h3>Coverage gaps</h3>${row('Connected accounts','3 / 3')}${row('Scanned RDS resources','36')}${row('Products with evidence','8')}${row('Unmatched resources',status('2 need ownership','amber'))}<div class="app-demo-notice">A provider failure produces missing/unknown evidence rather than a successful assessment.</div>${btn('Inspect collected evidence →','evidence-register','small blue')}</div></div>`,'Providers / AWS Network')}
function evidenceRegister(){return shell('evidence-register',`${topTitle('PLATFORM / EVIDENCE','Evidence Registry','Inspect verifiable observations, provenance, freshness and reuse across controls.',btn('Provider directory →','providers','blue'))}<div class="filterbar"><div class="filter">Product: All ⌄</div><div class="filter">Provider: All ⌄</div><div class="filter">Freshness: All ⌄</div><div class="filter">⌕ Search evidence…</div></div><div class="table-card"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>EVIDENCE ID</th><th>PRODUCT / RESOURCE</th><th>CAPABILITY</th><th>PROVIDER</th><th>TRUST</th><th>FRESHNESS</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['evi-2026-0172','customer-service / db-primary','net.internet-reachability','AWS Network','Verified','Fresh'],['evi-2026-0171','customer-service / db-primary','storage.encryption','AWS Config','Verified','Fresh'],['evi-2026-0168','billing-api / api','api.auth.scheme','OpenAPI','Verified','Fresh'],['evi-2026-0157','consent-service / customer-email','data.retention','No provider','Missing','Unknown']].map(r=>`<tr class="clickable" data-go="evidence-detail"><td><b class="link">${r[0]}</b></td><td>${r[1]}</td><td>${r[2]}</td><td>${r[3]}</td><td>${status(r[4],r[4]==='Verified'?'green':'amber')}</td><td>${status(r[5],r[5]==='Fresh'?'green':'amber')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><div class="help-inline">A single evidence observation may support several controls. Assessment results retain the pack version, evidence identity and exact product revision.</div>${nextCard('Examine the evidence trace','Inspect the observation and its trust information rather than relying on a green badge alone.','evidence-detail','View evidence →')}`,'Evidence / Registry')}
